const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is Queen Elizabeth National Park famous for?', a: 'Queen Elizabeth is most famous for its tree-climbing lions in the Ishasha sector and the Kazinga Channel boat cruise. It also has over 600 bird species — one of the highest counts of any park in Africa — and habituated chimpanzees in the Kyambura Gorge.' },
  { q: 'How far is Queen Elizabeth from Kampala?', a: 'Queen Elizabeth National Park is approximately 420km from Kampala, taking 5 to 6 hours by road via Mbarara. It is typically combined with Bwindi Impenetrable Forest (gorilla trekking) and Kibale Forest (chimpanzees) in multi-day safari circuits.' },
  { q: 'What is the best time to visit Queen Elizabeth National Park?', a: 'Game viewing is good year-round. The dry seasons from June to September and December to February offer easier game drives with shorter vegetation. The Kazinga Channel boat cruise is excellent in all seasons. The wet season brings lush landscapes and exceptional birding.' },
